<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46313" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">succŭba</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subc-</span></b> ), ae, comm.
		1. succubo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One who lies under;</i> hence, in mal. part., <i>a lecher</i> or <i>strumpet</i>
			(post-class.): florulentus,
			 Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ.</span> 10, 192;
			cf. 2. succubo.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a supplanter</i>,
				<i>rival</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 171, 31</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tori,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10</span></i>
			, p. 250, 18.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
